issue.description:
Proposed by phase bead sase-1tz.3.1.7 (tg_degraded, epic sase-1tz.3.1) as PROPOSED FOLLOW-UP #3; filed by the sase-1tz.3.1 land agent.

sase-telegram's hand-written `AGENTS.md` lists the package modules in its architecture section. Line 17 reads "`src/sase_telegram/credentials.py` — Bot token (via `pass`), chat ID and username (env vars)". The list does not mention:
- the new `src/sase_telegram/degraded.py`, which persists credential_unavailable and network_degraded outage states in `~/.sase/telegram/degraded_{outbound,receiver}.json`;
- the 60 s bot-token negative cache in `credentials.py` (`~/.sase/telegram/bot_token_unavailable.json`);
- the per-chunk retry and partial-delivery resume in `telegram_client.py` and outbound (`~/.sase/telegram/partial_delivery.json`), from sase-1tz.3.1.6.

The list is incomplete rather than false. Epic sase-1tz.3.1's plan authorized no AGENTS.md edits, so the phase left it alone. Add a one-line entry for degraded.py and extend the credentials.py and telegram_client.py lines.
